sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Kernel run execution and recovery
  accDescr: The Agent records a request, launches a per-run driver, streams model responses, applies policy, records tool intent before executing a tool, and projects every appended event. Approvals and restart recovery use the same ledger-driven loop.
  participant C as Caller / surface
  participant A as Agent API
  participant R as Run driver
  participant L as Append path + ledger
  participant P as Policy
  participant M as Model
  participant T as Tools

  C->>A: Start(input, profile, budget, principal)
  A->>A: Authorize, validate, deduplicate
  A->>L: fw.run.queued
  Note over A,L: Every event: emitMu → redact → Ledger.Append<br/>→ Run.Apply + wake status waiters → notify observers
  A->>R: Launch one driver, acquire root-run slot
  A-->>C: Run ID + current status
  R->>L: fw.run.started (brief, tools, model, zone)

  loop Until finished, waiting, canceled, or draining
    R->>R: Analyze events, build history<br/>Check budget and working time<br/>Compact context when needed
    R->>L: fw.turn.started + fw.model.requested
    R->>M: Stream(system, history, tool specs)
    M-->>R: Full response + usage + stop reason
    R->>L: fw.model.responded
    alt Response requests tools
      R->>R: Check allowlist, loop guard, call limits
      R->>P: Decide(tool, input, resolved input)
      P-->>R: Allow / Deny / Ask
      opt Ask requires a recorded decision
        R->>L: fw.approval.requested
        Note over C,R: Run is input-required, policy approval releases the driver
        C->>A: Decide(approval ID, decision)
        A->>L: fw.approval.decided
        A->>R: Relaunch if idle
      end
      alt Call is allowed
        R->>L: fw.tool.requested (idempotent flag)
        Note over R,L: File ledger fsyncs non-idempotent intent before the call
        L-->>R: Append succeeded
        R->>T: Call through input/output/timeout limits
        Note over R,T: Consecutive parallel-safe calls run together<br/>Questions, progress, and connection waits also emit events
        T-->>R: Bounded result
        R->>L: fw.tool.responded (batch results in request order)
      else Call is denied
        R->>L: fw.tool.responded (error result, no tool execution)
      end
      R->>L: fw.turn.finished
    else Final answer with no unseen follow-up
      R->>L: fw.turn.finished + fw.run.finished
    end
  end

  C->>A: Get / Wait / Events
  A-->>C: Projected run status or ledger event stream

  Note over A,T: Restart: rebuild status, idempotency keys, and child references from the ledger.<br/>Resume unfinished runs through the same driver. Pending approvals wait.<br/>Retry an unanswered model request or an idempotent tool.<br/>Other interrupted tools need approval, except supported continuations / connection waits.
